\description{
Fits, for each strategy, the model of artificial censoring (deviation from the strategy) used to
compute the inverse probability of censoring weights. Days are relative to the index date (day 0).
\itemize{
\item \code{"initiateWithin"} (grace period ending on day \code{G}): a binary model at \code{G}. The risk set holds the
persons with no outcome or death on or before day \code{G} (before day \code{G} with
\code{sameDayOrdering = "deviationFirst"}) and \code{riskEnd >= G}. The response is "started the treatment
on or before day \code{G}". The model is fit by \code{\link[CohortMethod:createPs]{CohortMethod::createPs()}} on a \code{CohortMethodData} view
of the risk set, so it gets CohortMethod's covariate tidying, high-correlation check, sampling
and regularization, and the AUC is computed with \code{\link[CohortMethod:computePsAuc]{CohortMethod::computePsAuc()}}.
\item \code{"notInitiateWithin"} and \code{"neverInitiate"}: a model of the hazard of initiation. Each person is
at risk of initiating from day 0 until the first of: initiation, the day before an outcome or
death (that day with \code{"deviationFirst"}), \code{riskEnd}, and the strategy's horizon \code{H} (\code{G}, or the
largest \code{riskEnd} for \code{"neverInitiate"}). Days outside this window are never part of the risk
set (structural zeros). With \code{hazardModelType = "cox"} there is one row per person with
time = last day at risk + 1, fit with a Cyclops Cox model and a Breslow baseline hazard, so the
probability of not initiating on days \verb{0..d} is \verb{S(d | X) = exp(-Lambda0(d + 1) exp(X beta))}.
With \code{hazardModelType = "logistic"} there is one row per person and interval of
\code{timeBasis$intervalLength} days (intervals counted from day 0, the last one ending at \code{H}), fit by
pooled logistic regression with an intercept, the time basis (never penalized) and the
covariates; \code{S(d | X)} is the product of \code{1 - h} over the intervals ending on or before day \code{d}.
With the indicator basis, an interval without initiations gets a hazard of 0, and an interval in
which everyone at risk initiates a hazard of 1 (the limits of the maximum likelihood fit). The rows
of these intervals are left out of the fit, and the first remaining interval is the reference.
With \code{covariateTimeInteraction = "day0"} or \code{"interval"}, the pooled logistic model also has the
products of the covariates with an indicator of the first interval, or with each time-basis
column, penalized like the covariates (see \code{\link[=createFitCensoringModelsArgs]{createFitCensoringModelsArgs()}}).
\item \code{"notInitiateWithin"} with \code{postGraceModel = "binary"} (the default): also the binary model at \code{G}
of an \code{"initiateWithin(G)"} strategy of the same treatment (shared with such a strategy when the
analysis has one), which gives the weights after \code{G} (see \code{\link[=createFitCensoringModelsArgs]{createFitCensoringModelsArgs()}}).
